# §8 part 2 — lateral usize↔u64 / size↔i64 implicit coercion
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT ENTERS (additive only; nothing removed — docs/design/mudancas-superficie-0.3.1.md §8):
#   - `same_word_lateral(a: PrimKind, b: PrimKind): bool` (`src/checker/expr.tks`, immediately after
#     `cast_is_lossless_widen`): true iff `{a,b}` is `{U64, Usize}` or `{I64, Size}` in EITHER order.
#     On teko's 64-bit-only target `usize` ≡ `u64` and `size` ≡ `i64` in BOTH width and sign — they
#     differ only in spelling — so each of those two pairs holds every value of its partner losslessly
#     in both directions. Deliberately limited to those two pairs: floats, `bool`, and the opaque §5
#     pointer words `uptr`/`ptr` are NOT lateral and stay explicit.
#   - WIRING: `same_word_lateral` becomes the FIRST check inside `cast_is_lossless_widen`
#     (`if same_word_lateral(inner, outer) { return true }`), the single source of truth. That reaches
#     BOTH the implicit-coercion gate (`numeric_widens_implicitly` → `widen_value_into` →
#     `coerce_value_into`, covering assignment/field/index/return) AND the fit-guard consumers (native
#     `lower_cast_fit_guard`, C `cast_may_lose`), so an implicit `u64`→`usize` relabel type-checks and
#     an explicit `u64 to usize` relabel correctly skips the runtime fit guard (same width = lossless,
#     lowered to a same-width no-op).
#   - ROOT CAUSE this closes: `int_arith_join` returns the LEFT kind on an equal-width tie, so it can
#     never report the RIGHT kind of such a pair as the join — `cast_is_lossless_widen` answered false
#     in BOTH directions for these two equal-width, same-sign, distinct-kind pairs, the sole gap left
#     by the pre-existing C#-style widening (a narrower same-sign int already widens implicitly, so
#     `u8`→`usize` and `i32`→`size` already worked). No other function changed: `int_arith_join`,
#     `prim_width`, `prim_is_signed` were already correct (Usize/Size → width 64; Usize unsigned, Size
#     signed).
#   - REDUNDANT-CAST PASS: UNCHANGED. Because `int_arith_join` returns the left operand on an
#     equal-width tie and `U64`≠`Usize` (and `I64`≠`Size`) at the enum level, `join_unchanged_without_cast`
#     never reports a lateral relabel as a no-op, so the D1 class-3 `redundant cast` diagnostic does
#     not fire on a deliberate `u64 to usize`/`i64 to size` relabel. Verified: a probe with
#     `(a to usize) + b` and `(a to u64) < b` builds with NO redundant-cast warning.
#   - NO runtime C touched. NO `.tkb` wire change (the emitted corpus spells no new construct).
